// lib/succession — Primary and alternate officeholder succession (`D34`, `#40`, `#62`):
// - The primary officeholder serves while available; if unavailable (declined, incapacitated,
//   or deceased), the alternate automatically steps in via `Default` / `Exception`.

Module role-succession(office, person) {

  Function primary-for Identified by office * person
  Function alternate-for Identified by office * person
  Fact unavailable Identified by person

  Fact acting-holder Identified by office * person
    Default primary-serves
      Holds when primary-for(office, person)
    Exception primary-unavailable Overrides primary-serves
      Rejects when primary-for(office, person) && unavailable(person)
    Default alternate-serves
      Holds when alternate-for(office, person)
        && (Exists person': primary-for(office, person') && unavailable(person'))
        && !unavailable(person)

  Act mark-unavailable Actor person
    Holds when !unavailable(person)
    Creates unavailable(person)

  Invariant single-acting-holder When
    !(Exists office, person, person':
      person != person' && acting-holder(office, person) && acting-holder(office, person'))

}
